e":0.6784,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"TEN","distance":0.6905,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"NO","distance":0.6958,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Pete Carmichael"},{"season":2022,"team":"PIT","distance":0.7678,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"ARI","distance":0.7985,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Drew Petzing"}],"defense":[{"season":2022,"team":"DET","distance":0.362,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2024,"team":"DET","distance":0.4689,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2023,"team":"CLE","distance":0.4744,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.4785,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2025,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.5192,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Giants are 4-2-1 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 163 to 161. The offense ranks 14th in EPA per play and the defense 18th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. What sets them apart is the lowest pre-snap motion rate and the 2nd highest eight man box rate in the league.","offense":"The Giants offense has been a little above average by EPA per play so far. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the lowest pre-snap motion rate and the 2nd most backs in the backfield in the league. Jameis Winston has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Malik Nabers, who has drawn 30% of the targets.","defense":"The Giants defense has been about average by EPA allowed per play so far. Even its strongest area, success rate allowed, only ranks 14th, and it is 29th in sack rate. Abdul Carter has led the way with 2 sacks. Schematically, they have the 2nd highest eight man box rate in the league.","special":"The Giants have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 72% of field goals, which is well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into linebackers, about 21% of the money on the books. Their defensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"The quarterback job has been split, with Jameis Winston and J.J. McCarthy both getting meaningful snaps. Malik Nabers has been the clear top target with 30% of the looks and 605 receiving yards. Cam Skattebo has handled most of the work in the backfield with 58% of the carries. On defense, Abdul Carter leads the team with 2 sacks and Jevon Holland has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Matt Nagy is calling the offense and Dennard Wilson is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Broncos and the 2024 Titans. Their defense looks most like the 2022 and 2024 Lions, both under Aaron Glenn.","trends":"The offense went from 17th in EPA per play in 2025 to 14th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 25th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 18th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was RPO rate, which went from 12% to 3%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}